          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.3. A number for which the sum of all its factors is equal to twice the number is called a perfect number. The number 28 is a perfect number. Its factors are 1, 2, 4, 7, 14 and 28. Their sum is 56 which is twice 28. Find a perfect number between 1 and 10.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.148,
            0.2,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.175,
            0.492,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.4. Find the common factors of: a. 20 and 28 b. 35 and 50 c. 4, 8 and 12 d. 5, 15 and 25",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.257,
            0.531,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. a. Common factors of 20 and 28 = 1, 2, 4. b. Common factors of 35 and 50 = 1, 5. c. Common factors of 4, 8 and 12 = 1, 2, 4. d. Common factors of 5, 15 and 25 = 1, 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.337,
            0.78,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.5. Find any three numbers that are multiples of 25 but not multiples of 50.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.364,
            0.528,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Some such numbers are: 25, 75, 125, 175."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.391,
            0.883,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.6. Anshu and his friends play the ‘idli-vada’ game with two numbers, which are both smaller than 10. The first time anybody says ‘idlivada’ is after the number 50. What could the two numbers be which are assigned ‘idli’ and ‘vada’?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.454,
            0.391,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. 7, 8 8, 9 (Try for other possibility)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.535,
            0.881,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.7. In the treasure hunting game, Grumpy has kept treasures on 28 and 70. What jump sizes will land on both the numbers?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.58,
            0.44,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. The jump sizes are 1, 2, 7 or 14"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.607,
            0.883,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.8. In the diagram below, Guna has erased all the numbers except the common multiples. Find out what those numbers could be and fill in the missing numbers in the empty regions.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.67,
            0.352,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Multiples of 3 Think of some more."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.54,
            0.67,
            0.662,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Multiples of 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.724,
            0.882,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.9. Find the smallest number that is a multiple of all the numbers from 1 to 10 except for 7.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.769,
            0.215,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. 360"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.796,
            0.813,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.10. Find the smallest number that is a multiple of all the number from 1 to 10.",
